The attempt to use `kubectl edit` failed because the editor `vi` was not available in the sandbox environment. This means I cannot perform an interactive edit.

I must perform a strategic update using `kubectl patch` or by applying a new configuration, assuming I can reconstruct the YAML or patch the existing one.

Since I do not have the original YAML, and I cannot interact with a file editor, I will try to patch the deployment directly to inject the necessary volumes and mounts.

I will patch the deployment `app` to add a temporary volume and mount it to common locations where applications write data (e.g., `/var/log/nginx` and `/tmp`).

Patch command structure:
1. Define the `volumes` under `spec.template.spec.volumes`.
2. Define the `volumeMounts` under `spec.template.spec.containers[0].volumeMounts`.

I will use a JSON merge patch for this. I will assume the application is Nginx based on the pod description.

Patch target:
```json
{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "volumes": [
          {
            "name": "log-volume",
            "emptyDir": {}
          }
        ],
        "containers": [
          {
            "name": "app",
            "volumeMounts": [
              {
                "name": "log-volume",
                "mountPath": "/var/log/nginx"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```
I will apply this patch to the `app` deployment in the `default` namespace.

